<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Induction</title>
  <handout>
    <title>Recursive Counting</title>
    <p workspace="2cm">
      What do you need to know about lattice path problems?
    </p>  
    <p workspace="4cm">
      Consider the expansion of <m>(3+x^{5}+y+xy^{3})^{50}</m>. Find the coefficient on each of the following terms.
      <ol marker="a." cols="3">
        <li>
          <p>
            <m>x^{30}y^{4}</m>
          </p>
        </li>
        
        <li>
          <p>
            <m>x^{3}y^{3}</m>
          </p>
        </li>
        
        <li>
          <p>
            <m>x^{30}y^{15}</m>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </p>
    <p workspace="4cm">
      How can we interpret the notation <m>1+2+\cdots + n^2</m>?
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Peer instruction question 1</alert>
    </p>
    <p workspace="7cm">
      <me>
        \binom{n}{k} = \binom{n-1}{k-1} + \binom{n-1}{k}
      </me>
      
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Peer instruction question 2</alert>
    </p>
    <p>
      Let <m>r(n)</m> be the number of regions determined by <m>n</m> lines in the plane drawn so that each pair intersects but no three lines intersect at a single point.
    </p>
    <sidebyside widths="25% 75%">
      <tabular>
        <row bottom="minor">
          <cell><m>n</m></cell>
          <cell><m>r(n)</m></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>0</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>1</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>2</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>3</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>4</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>
      <p>
        <nbsp/>
      </p>
    </sidebyside>
    <p workspace="10cm">
      
    </p>
  </handout>
</chapter>
